**Lord Wellesley** brought in the **Subsidiary Alliance**. Think of a security guard you must pay, who then runs your house.

A ruler who signed it:
- accepted the British as the **supreme power**;
- kept **British troops** in his state, **at his own cost**;
- accepted a **British Resident** at his court;
- made **no treaties or wars** with others without the British;
- so he **lost his independence**.

Your textbook names **Awadh** as the first such state (Treaty of Allahabad, 1765). Others were **Hyderabad**, **Mysore**, **Tanjore** and some **Rajput states**.

**Model answer.** *What was the Subsidiary Alliance? Name two states under it.*

- A system of **Lord Wellesley**: a ruler paid for **British troops** in his state and lost control of his foreign affairs.
- Two states: **Hyderabad** and **Awadh**.

A structured question in three parts. Write your answer first, then open the box.

*Economic hardship was a big cause of the revolt. Explain:*
- (a) how Indian handicrafts were ruined (3 marks);
- (b) how peasants were made poorer (3 marks);
- (c) how India's economy was made to serve Britain (4 marks).

*1857 changed how India was ruled. Explain:*
- (a) the changes in the government of India (3 marks);
- (b) the changes in the army (3 marks);
- (c) the new policy towards the princes (4 marks).
